<% content_for :title, "Agentic Log — Kevin Skilton" %>

<section class="hero-panel">
  <div class="hero-badges">
    <span class="badge badge-cyan">Design + AI</span>
    <span class="badge badge-slate">Product-focused</span>
    <span class="badge badge-fuchsia">UI review</span>
  </div>

  <p class="section-kicker">Agentic design workflow</p>
  <h1 class="hero-title">A richer page for agentic UI delivery.</h1>
  <p class="hero-copy">The agentic log now includes a LinkedIn influencer role that reviews page feel, suggests UI polish, and shapes the product handoff before the team builds the final experience.</p>

  <div class="hero-grid">
    <div class="card-panel accent-card">
      <p class="card-kicker">Influencer role</p>
      <h2 class="card-title">Design guidance before code</h2>
      <p class="card-copy">A design-focused agent aligns the interface with modern UI standards, recommending color, spacing, and typography improvements so the final page looks professional from the start.</p>
      <div class="pill-row">
        <span class="pill pill-cyan">Elevated spacing</span>
        <span class="pill pill-fuchsia">Brand color</span>
        <span class="pill pill-emerald">Content rhythm</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card-panel">
      <p class="card-kicker">Visual polish</p>
      <h3 class="card-title">Stronger contrast, structure, and motion</h3>
      <p class="card-copy">The page now balances a confident dark brand palette with crisp cards and badge elements so the workflow feels curated, not generic.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="content-panel">
  <div class="content-stack">
    <p class="section-kicker">Flow</p>
    <h2 class="panel-title">Agent → Influencer → Team → User</h2>
    <p class="panel-copy">This workflow blends product signals with visual direction so the output is both functional and polished before it reaches production.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="flow-grid">
    <div class="card-panel small-card">
      <span class="step-pill step-cyan">Step 1</span>
      <h3 class="card-title">Intent captured</h3>
      <p class="card-copy">A need, bug, or feature request becomes a clear product prompt.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card-panel small-card">
      <span class="step-pill step-fuchsia">Step 2</span>
      <h3 class="card-title">Influencer review</h3>
      <p class="card-copy">A design agent reviews color, spacing, and experience before the code is written.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card-panel small-card">
      <span class="step-pill step-emerald">Step 3</span>
      <h3 class="card-title">Task generation</h3>
      <p class="card-copy">The agent breaks work into tasks and routes it to the right contributors.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card-panel small-card">
      <span class="step-pill step-amber">Step 4</span>
      <h3 class="card-title">Build and ship</h3>
      <p class="card-copy">Developers implement the experience with the influencer’s visual direction in mind.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="note-box">
    <div class="note-title">Design coordination</div>
    <p>The influencer role keeps the experience consistent and polished at every handoff.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="info-grid">
    <div class="card-panel">
      <p class="card-kicker">Design signal</p>
      <h3 class="card-title">Feedback before code</h3>
      <p class="card-copy">The influencer defines whether the page feels intuitive and modern before implementation begins.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-panel">
      <p class="card-kicker">Visual rhythm</p>
      <h3 class="card-title">Hierarchy and polish</h3>
      <p class="card-copy">Spacing, typography, and color choices are guided by design review.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-panel">
      <p class="card-kicker">Production quality</p>
      <h3 class="card-title">Refined handoff</h3>
      <p class="card-copy">Every release is reviewed for visual impact and clarity before it reaches the user.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
